---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Src from '../components/Src.astro';
import Aff from '../components/Aff.astro';
import Unverified from '../components/Unverified.astro';
const S = {
  smPrice: 'https://www.mysmartmove.com/pricing',
  smDisc: 'https://www.mysmartmove.com/disclaimer',
  ttScreen: 'https://www.turbotenant.com/tenant-screening/',
  ttHelpCost: 'https://support.turbotenant.com/en/articles/6362365-what-s-the-difference-between-a-rental-application-and-a-screening-report',
  ttHelpRead: 'https://support.turbotenant.com/en/articles/4409356-how-do-i-read-a-tenant-screening-report',
  rrPrice: 'https://rentredi.com/pricing/',
  rrScreen: 'https://rentredi.com/tenant-screening/',
  rentec: 'https://www.rentecdirect.com/pricing-transparency',
  rp: 'https://rentprep.com/guide/packages-pricing/',
};
const title = 'Tenant Screening Reports Compared: What Each One Actually Includes';
const description = 'SmartMove, TurboTenant, RentRedi, Rentec Direct and RentPrep side by side: price, who pays, what is in each report, and the state-by-state gaps each provider discloses. Quoted from their own pages.';
const schema = {"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Article","headline":title,"description":description,"dateModified":"2026-11-18"};
---
<Base title={title} description={description} schema={schema}>
  <h1>{title}</h1>
  <p class="lede">Most comparisons stop at price. The bigger difference is what comes back, and in which states. Every figure below is from the provider's own pricing or help page as of November 18, 2026, and each one links to it.</p>

  <h2>Side by side</h2>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table>
    <thead><tr><th>Provider</th><th>Price (as published)</th><th>Who pays</th><th>What's included</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>TransUnion SmartMove</strong></td>
        <td>Basic $25 · Plus $42 · Premium $49, plus tax where applicable; income verification add-on $11 <Src href={S.smPrice} /></td>
        <td>Landlord or applicant ("where permitted") <Src href={S.smPrice} /></td>
        <td>Basic: ResidentScore + criminal. Plus: adds credit report and eviction-related report. Premium: adds Income Estimator and Identity Check <Src href={S.smPrice} /></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>TurboTenant</strong></td>
        <td>$55 on the Free plan, $45 on Essentials/Pro <Src href={S.ttHelpCost} /></td>
        <td>Applicant by default; landlord can choose to pay <Src href={S.ttScreen} /></td>
        <td>TransUnion credit report and score, nationwide criminal background check, eviction check covering all 50 states <Src href={S.ttScreen} /></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>RentRedi</strong></td>
        <td>$39.99 credit + criminal + eviction; $49.99 with Plaid income verification <Src href={S.rrPrice} /></td>
        <td>Tenant-paid <Src href={S.rrPrice} /></td>
        <td>TransUnion credit (ResidentScore), criminal, eviction; Plaid income verification on the higher tier <Src href={S.rrScreen} /></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Rentec Direct</strong></td>
        <td>Basic $14.95 / Enhanced $20.95 / Premium $29.45 on Starter; $10 / $13 / $18 on Pro &amp; PM plans <Src href={S.rentec} /></td>
        <td>Not stated on the pricing page <Unverified /></td>
        <td>Basic: nationwide criminal, sex offender, SSN validation. Enhanced: adds nationwide eviction search. Premium: adds TransUnion credit report and score <Src href={S.rentec} /></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>RentPrep</strong></td>
        <td>Credit Report Only $29 · Full Background Check Only $29 · Complete Screening Package $49; income add-ons $10 / $15 <Src href={S.rp} /></td>
        <td>Credit-only and Complete: landlord or tenant. Background-only: landlord pays only <Src href={S.rp} /></td>
        <td>Credit-only is "the automated SmartMove package" (credit report, ResidentScore, bankruptcies). Background-only and Complete add an FCRA-certified screener review, SSN verification, nationwide criminal and sex offender, nationwide evictions, judgments and liens <Src href={S.rp} /></td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
  <p class="meta">Monthly software fees are separate and not shown here. RentRedi, Rentec Direct and TurboTenant's paid tiers each have their own subscription prices on their pricing pages.</p>

  <h2>The gap the price table hides: coverage by state</h2>
  <p>A "nationwide criminal check" doesn't return the same records everywhere. State and local laws restrict what can be reported, and providers handle that differently. Here is what each one discloses.</p>

  <h3>SmartMove publishes its list</h3>
  <p>TransUnion SmartMove's disclaimer page says that, as of its January 14, 2026 revision, <strong>criminal records are available to return in 30 states</strong>: Alaska, Arizona, Arkansas, Colorado, Connecticut, Florida, Georgia, Illinois, Indiana, Iowa, Kansas, Louisiana, Maryland, Minnesota, Missouri, Nebraska, New Jersey, New Mexico, North Carolina, North Dakota, Ohio, Oklahoma, Oregon, Pennsylvania, Rhode Island, Tennessee, Texas, Utah, Washington, and Wisconsin <Src href={S.smDisc} />.</p>
  <p>The same page (revised August 12, 2026) says <strong>eviction records are not available</strong> in Kentucky, Louisiana, Maine, South Dakota and Wyoming, and are <strong>limited</strong> in California, Connecticut, Georgia, Hawaii, Idaho, Illinois, Michigan, Mississippi, Missouri, Montana, Nevada, New Mexico, Ohio, Pennsylvania, Tennessee, Texas, Washington, West Virginia and Wisconsin <Src href={S.smDisc} />.</p>
  <p>It also requires a <strong>phased screening</strong> (non-criminal bundle first, criminal only after the applicant meets preliminary criteria) in Ann Arbor, MI; Berkeley, CA; Cook County, IL; Detroit, MI; Maryland (statewide); New Jersey (statewide); New York City; Oakland, CA; and Washington, D.C. (revised October 1, 2026) <Src href={S.smDisc} />.</p>

  <h3>TurboTenant describes it in its help center</h3>
  <p>TurboTenant says its criminal checks go through TransUnion and "cover all 50 states," but that reports are "subject to State Suppression Laws": look-back limits in states like Colorado and New York, and dismissed or expunged cases left out in places like Massachusetts and Hawaii <Src href={S.ttHelpRead} />. In Cook County, IL; Detroit, MI; Montgomery County, MD; Oakland, CA; Berkeley, CA; and Washington, D.C., TurboTenant says results "will indicate whether records exist, but specific charge details will not be provided," because it does not support the two-phase process there <Src href={S.ttHelpRead} />. See our explainer on <a href="/turbotenant-no-criminal-records-available/">"No criminal records are available"</a>.</p>

  <h3>RentRedi, Rentec Direct and RentPrep</h3>
  <p>We did not find a state-by-state coverage list on the pages we reviewed for these three <Unverified note="not yet found" />. RentRedi's and RentPrep's credit products run on TransUnion (RentRedi says it partners with TransUnion <Src href={S.rrScreen} />; RentPrep calls its credit-only product "the automated SmartMove package" <Src href={S.rp} />). We have not confirmed whether SmartMove's criminal-coverage limits also apply to their criminal searches, so treat that as an open question.</p>

  <h2>How to choose, by situation</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Your rental is in a state missing from SmartMove's criminal list</strong> (for example California, New York, Massachusetts or Virginia): ask any provider, in writing, whether its criminal search returns records for your county before you charge an applicant. Our <a href="/application-fee-caps-by-state/">fee-cap table</a> shows what you're allowed to charge.</li>
    <li><strong>You're in a phased-screening jurisdiction</strong> (Cook County, NYC, D.C., New Jersey, Maryland and the others listed above): you'll need a two-step workflow. SmartMove supports it; TurboTenant says it doesn't, and instead shows whether records exist without the charge details <Src href={S.smDisc} label="SM" /><Src href={S.ttHelpRead} label="TT" />.</li>
    <li><strong>You want a person to review the background results:</strong> RentPrep lists an "FCRA-Certified Screener Review" in its background and complete packages <Src href={S.rp} />.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>If an applicant offers a report they already paid for, check whether your state makes you accept it or waive the fee: <a href="/reusable-tenant-screening-reports-by-state/">reusable reports by state</a>.</p>

  <p>Deciding who pays? Run the numbers with the <a href="/tenant-screening-cost-calculator/">screening cost calculator</a>. In a two-step jurisdiction, see <a href="/phased-tenant-screening-jurisdictions/">phased screening rules</a>; to double-check an eviction section, use the <a href="/eviction-records-official-court-portals/">official court portals</a>.</p>

  <p>Coming from the free-for-landlords screening in Zillow Rental Manager? See <a href="/alternatives-to-zillow-rental-manager-screening/">alternatives to Zillow screening</a> for what it includes and who pays on each option.</p>

